    <string name="share_text">Map of EV charging stations in Kyrgyzstan: see which ports are free.</string>

    <string name="banner_offline">No connection — showing the last loaded map. Addresses, connectors and prices are correct, but how many ports are free right now is unknown.</string>
    <string name="banner_stale">%1$d stations have stale availability — their network is not responding. They are shown in grey: addresses and prices are correct, the number of free ports is unknown.</string>
    <string name="banner_no_connection">No connection. Check the internet and refresh — the map appears as soon as the server answers.</string>
    <string name="banner_error">Could not refresh the data: %1$s</string>
    <string name="banner_error_cached">Could not refresh the data: %1$s. Showing the last loaded copy.</string>

    <string name="about_title">About</string>
    <string name="about_intro">A map of EV charging stations in Kyrgyzstan. It shows which ports are free right now, so you do not drive to an occupied charger.</string>
    <string name="about_source_h">Where the data comes from</string>
    <string name="about_source1">From the apps of four networks: SPARK, We way, EVION and Charge24. This app is not affiliated with them and sells nothing — it only gathers their maps into one.</string>
    <string name="about_source2">Availability is refreshed every five minutes. Between refreshes the picture can lag: a charger taken a minute ago is still shown as free.</string>
    <string name="about_pin_h">The station marker</string>
    <string name="about_pin1">The ring is split by the number of ports: green — free, red — busy, grey — offline. The centre shows the total number of ports.</string>
    <string name="about_pin2">If a network stops responding, the ring turns entirely grey: showing stale availability as current would be misleading.</string>
    <string name="about_price_h">Prices</string>
    <string name="about_price">Shown exactly as the networks report them. Time-of-day discounts are not part of that data — check the network\'s own app.</string>
